  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197900: PostgreSQL Linux x86 matrix and full pool soak

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Linux x86_64 is directly qualified for released PostgreSQL majors 14, 15 and
17, in addition to Linux arm64 and macOS arm64. The weekly soak's complete
3,000-operation workload is also locally executable evidence, not only a future
CI schedule. Its Wasm fuel remains bounded by a host formula: five million base
instructions plus ten thousand per authorized worker operation.

## Evidence

A single clean Debian Bookworm amd64 container using Temurin 21.0.11 passed the
complete interoperability program against PostgreSQL 14.23, 15.18 and 17.10.
On macOS arm64, PostgreSQL 17.9 completed 1,000 acquire/query/reset/release
operations from each of three concurrent guest workers through two connections.
All leases, waiters and native handles terminate empty. Disposable containers,
cache volumes and OrbStack were cleaned up.

This closes the requested released-version/platform matrix and full scheduled
soak implementation evidence. CI remains a freshness gate, not an unimplemented
functional gap.")))
